From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 01:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] catalystwan: expose the vEdge Cloud certificate authority

vManage keeps TWO certificate-authority settings and this module only ever
exposed one:

  /settings/configuration/certificate   -> the CONTROLLERS (vManage/vBond/vSmart)
  /settings/configuration/vedgecloud    -> vEdge Cloud, i.e. VIRTUAL EDGES

Measured on a live 20.18.4 fabric that our own lane had just brought up, with
all three controller certificates installed against an enterprise root CA:

    certificate  certificate_signing  = 'enterprise'   <- our lane sets this
    vedgecloud   certificateauthority = 'cisco'        <- nothing sets this
    enterprise root CA: installed, control_connection_up: True

So a fabric we deliberately moved onto an enterprise CA was still telling any
virtual edge to expect CISCO-signed certificates. That is not a preference, it
is an inconsistency in a fabric we configure end to end, and it is invisible
because no surface reports it.

The SDK has had both halves all along -- `get_vedge_cloud` / `edit_vedge_cloud`
and the one-field `VEdgeCloud` model -- so this exposes the capability rather
than adding one. Same shape as 0003: the endpoint existed, the module did not
surface it.

HONEST SCOPE. Setting this to `enterprise` does NOT, by itself, let a virtual
edge into the WAN edge list. Measured immediately after flipping it, both
inventory lanes refused exactly as before:

    .csv     -> 'Virtual Platform is not allowed in CSV Upload.'  (VELIST0001)
    .viptela -> 'Disallowed ENG cert. Failed to verify signature.'(VELIST0001)

Those are lane restrictions and a Cisco engineering signature respectively, and
neither is governed by this setting. This patch fixes a real misconfiguration;
it does not claim to onboard an edge.

Controls (the module source, against the installed SDK):

  PASS argspec has vedge_cloud          PASS uses SDK edit_vedge_cloud
  PASS option certificate_authority     PASS uses SDK get_vedge_cloud
  PASS VEdgeCloud imported              PASS modify flag initialised
  PASS controllers path untouched  (edit_certificates still called exactly once)

  SDK: get_vedge_cloud True, edit_vedge_cloud True, VEdgeCloud fields
       ['certificateauthority']

The comparison follows the existing read-then-diff pattern, so an already
correct fabric reports no change rather than re-writing the setting every run.

UPSTREAM ASK: FILE. A plain capability gap against
cisco-en-programmability/ansible-collection-catalystwan.

---
diff --git a/plugins/modules/administration_settings.py b/plugins/modules/administration_settings.py
--- a/plugins/modules/administration_settings.py
+++ b/plugins/modules/administration_settings.py
@@ -206,6 +206,7 @@
 
 from catalystwan.endpoints.configuration_settings import (
     Certificate,
+    VEdgeCloud,
     Device,
     OnOffMode,
     Organization,
@@ -248,6 +249,22 @@
                 port=dict(type="str"),
             ),
         ),
+        vedge_cloud=dict(
+            # The VIRTUAL-edge certificate authority, which is a DIFFERENT
+            # setting from `certificates` above. `certificates` governs the
+            # CONTROLLERS (vManage/vBond/vSmart); this one governs vEdge Cloud
+            # devices, and vManage keeps them independently -- measured on a
+            # live 20.18.4 fabric whose controllers were already 'enterprise'
+            # while this still read 'cisco'.
+            type="dict",
+            aliases=["vedge_cloud_certificate_authorization"],
+            options=dict(
+                certificate_authority=dict(
+                    type="str",
+                    choices=["cisco", "manual", "enterprise"],
+                ),
+            ),
+        ),
         certificates=dict(
             type="dict",
             aliases=["cca", "controler_certificate_authorization"],
@@ -313,6 +330,7 @@
     modify_vbond = False
     modify_org = False
     modify_certificates = False
+    modify_vedge_cloud = False
     modify_enterprise_root_ca = False
     modify_smart_account_credentials = False
     modify_pnp_sync = False
@@ -359,6 +377,15 @@
         ).single_or_default()
         modify_certificates = True if certificates_data != certificates_payload else False
 
+    if module.params.get("vedge_cloud"):
+        vedge_cloud_payload = VEdgeCloud(
+            certificateauthority=module.params.get("vedge_cloud").get("certificate_authority")
+        )
+        vedge_cloud_data = module.get_response_safely(
+            module.session.endpoints.configuration_settings.get_vedge_cloud
+        ).single_or_default()
+        modify_vedge_cloud = True if vedge_cloud_data != vedge_cloud_payload else False
+
     if module.params.get("enterprise_root_ca"):
         if not HAS_ENTERPRISE_ROOT_CA_ENDPOINT:
             module.fail_json(
@@ -431,6 +458,15 @@
             response_key="certificates",
         )
 
+    if modify_vedge_cloud:
+        module.send_request_safely(
+            result,
+            action_name="Administration Settings: vEdge Cloud Certificate Authorization",
+            send_func=module.session.endpoints.configuration_settings.edit_vedge_cloud,
+            payload=vedge_cloud_payload,
+            response_key="vedge_cloud",
+        )
+
     if modify_enterprise_root_ca:
         module.send_request_safely(
             result,
